## 5. Historical Position

Bu Theory stands in a long lineage of "local exceptions" to classical rigidity:

| Tradition | Local exception | Global claim |
|-----------|----------------|--------------|
| Leibniz | infinitesimals | not a new arithmetic |
| Hegel | dialectical becoming | not formalised |
| Robinson | hyperreals | zero still has no inverse |
| Lawvere / Kock | synthetic differential geometry | smooth only, not global |
| Colombeau | generalized functions | products defined only up to equivalence |
| Hadamard | finite part | a prescription, not a field |
| **Bu Theory** | **every point is a germ** | **a globally connected arithmetic world** |

Every predecessor permits a **local** crossing of the classical boundary.
Bu Theory is the first framework to declare the boundary crossed **globally**,
while using projection to remain compatible with classical mathematics at the
interface.

---

## 6. What Bu Theory Does *Not* Claim

To prevent misunderstanding, the philosophical boundaries are explicit:

- ❌ It is **not** a claim that `0 = 1` in classical Boolean logic.
- ❌ It is **not** a denial of classical arithmetic or analysis.
- ❌ It is **not** a proof of the consistency of arithmetic.
- ❌ It is **not** a rejection of rigor — only a relocation of where rigor
  applies.

What it **does** claim:

- ✅ Classical mathematics is the **first projective layer** of a richer system.
- ✅ Contradiction can be **encapsulated** rather than **exploded**.
- ✅ A globally connected arithmetic can exist **without violating** the
  classical interface wherever that interface is defined.

---

## 7. Status of This Document

This repository is an **exploratory research programme**, not a formally
verified treatise.

The five open problems listed in `OPEN-PROBLEMS.md` are genuine:

1. **ZF Model of ϑ** — can the germ be constructed as a set-theoretic object?
2. **Projection Formalization** — can π be given a clean categorical definition?
3. **Depth Rigor** — can generation depth support transfinite constructions?
4. **Prime Interface** — can residual order be linked to primality?
5. **Relative Consistency** — is there a non-trivial model of all axioms?

Acknowledging these gaps is part of the philosophy:

> **To declare the foundation is not to claim it is finished.**
> **It is to state clearly where the work begins.**

---

## 8. One-Paragraph Summary (for citation)

> Bu Theory adopts dialectical logic as its internal reasoning engine.
> Classical formal logic is not rejected; it is demoted to an external
> projection interface (π), where contradictions are encapsulated and do not
> propagate. Every real point is treated as a point-germ carrying an internal
> identification `0 ≃ 1`; the manifestation projection releases only controlled
> residues into the classical layer. This is not a violation of logic — it is a
> **stratification of logic itself**: dialectical at the root, formal at the
> interface.

